    Bug 1912022 - Fix _execute_browser_action command in menus API. r=aleca

    Found to be not working while investigating bug 1911752. Will add a
    dedicated test for this in bug 1912021.

    This seems to be a left-over from the time when the mail tab was split
    into sub windows (or it never worked). A mouse click event on the folder
    pane or message pane is passing the `about:3pane` window and the
    detection code for the unified toolbar (see [1]) fails. The action is
    therefore not triggered.

    [1]: https://searchfox.org/comm-central/rev/4010d287c4585532f986b886f4bccad478a1455a/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-browserAction.js#61

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D218731

diff --git a/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-menus.js b/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-menus.js
index 068645f1ee3..277e92c0613 100644
--- a/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-menus.js
+++ b/mail/components/extensions/parent/ext-menus.js
@@ -469,7 +469,7 @@ var gMenuBuilder = {
         }[item.command];
         if (actionFor) {
           const win = event.target.ownerGlobal;
-          actionFor(item.extension).triggerAction(win);
+          actionFor(item.extension).triggerAction(win.top);
           return;
         }
